## Design

`query_*.py` files are named by **call pattern** — what the module does at the
API call level — not by method value. This is the right axis because
`query_rag.py` and `query_per_fuel.py` share the same method (`rag`) but
implement distinct call patterns (single bulk call vs 3 sub-calls by fuel type).

## File rename table

| Current                | New                      | Call pattern                          |
|------------------------|--------------------------|---------------------------------------|
| `query_frontier.py`    | `query_direct.py`        | Single call, no retrieval context     |
| `query_rag.py`         | `query_rag.py`           | Bulk curated corpus injection (stays) |
| `query_decomposed.py`  | `query_per_fuel.py`      | 3 sub-calls split by fuel type        |
| `query_web.py`         | `query_livesearch.py`    | Live Tavily search injection          |
| `query_multiturn.py`   | `query_multiturn.py`     | Multi-turn with accumulated history   |
| `query_verification.py`| `query_verification.py`  | 5-mode verification overlay           |
| `query_fusion.py`      | `query_fusion.py`        | Fusion pipeline (separate arch)       |

`query_sourced.py` does not exist on disk — the `sourced` sweep used `query_rag.py`
with `prompt_cited.txt`. No rename needed.

## Actions

1. `git mv query_frontier.py query_direct.py`
2. `git mv query_decomposed.py query_per_fuel.py`
3. `git mv query_web.py query_livesearch.py`
4. Update all import sites: `harness.py`, `manager.py`, `__init__.py`,
   and any script that imports from these modules (grep before editing).
5. Update the one-line module docstring in each renamed file to state
   its call pattern in plain language.
6. Run `make test` green.

## Exit criteria

- No file named `query_frontier.py`, `query_decomposed.py`, or `query_web.py`
  in `src/aedist/`.
- All imports updated; `make test` green.
- Each `query_*.py` has a one-line docstring stating its call pattern.
- Unblocks 0125.


